<!-- FIXTURE
proves: a genuinely indented code block at TOP level is still blanked.
Repetition inside code is routinely correct — this repo's own kiro wrapper
carries `--bind /usr/local /usr/local` — so scanning it would be a
tokenization bug, not a finding. The `echo` line is the discriminating
case: it is a doubling the scanner WOULD report anywhere else, so its
absence from the expectations is what proves the block was blanked. The
closing paragraph is the positive control; without it this fixture would
pass just as happily if the scanner never opened the file.
expect: 20 "the the"
-->

# Indented code at top level

An ordinary paragraph, then a blank line, then four columns of code:

    kiro --bind /usr/local /usr/local --bind /run /run
    echo the the

This closing paragraph is ordinary prose, and the the doubling in it must
be reported.
